# Rust sources are LF, always.
#
# `rustfmt.toml` sets `newline_style = "Unix"`, so a CRLF `.rs` file fails
# `cargo fmt --check` — and with `core.autocrlf = true` a clone can rewrite
# LF files to CRLF on checkout without anyone editing them. Pinning the
# attribute here makes the gate's outcome independent of each clone's
# configuration rather than a property of whoever committed last.
#
# Scoped to `.rs` on purpose. `src/hoarfrost/spec.md` is also stored with
# CRLF, but nothing gates on it and requirement files are not to be
# rewritten as a side effect of a formatting fix.
*.rs text eol=lf

# Gallery screenshots are documentation, and a mangled byte makes a broken
# image rather than a diff someone can read. Declared binary so no
# checkout-time line-ending rule ever touches them.
*.png binary
